## Scope of the accepted component

The new supplied-byte manifest validator and bounded read-only content verifier
are accepted as source-tested components. The local exact suite passed **89
tests in 0.059 seconds**, with exact-file Ruff clean. The source CI includes these
89 tests and the unchanged accepted Linux isolation/CPU regressions. New verifier
tree tests use generated bytes and a runtime-guard double; runtime guard tests
use explicit doubles. Native pre-ML release-gate integration is **not** established
by those synthetic tests alone.

The external manifest pin, explicit caller budgets, exact tree/role/content
checks, per-object stability observations and descriptor cleanup are covered.
Receipts never grant execution. They explicitly do not prove runtime publisher
origin, complete dynamic dependencies, a coherent point-in-time snapshot,
execution-time immutability or real-host binding. A regression documents the
earlier-file mutation limit rather than claiming a mutable scan is a snapshot.
The trusted-host/local-filesystem premises and cooperative deadline limitations
are recorded in v0.45 and the module docstrings.

