## Roadmap and next work

**This release-verification component step is complete. Gate 5 overall remains
partial.** The next finite integration is to enforce verification at the existing
guardian release boundary, before its `b"G"` message can unblock the CPU worker.
The existing cgroup guardian release callback and IPC/WorkerRun composition
provide the boundary; no new blanket hostile-host sandbox gate is required.

Use a fresh remote-Linux generated integration successor while preserving the
accepted fixtures. Assert positive pre-ML verification before release; wrong
external pin and same-size tamper must produce zero release/WorkerRun calls and
fixed failures with complete cleanup. Preserve the accepted lifecycle and
generated CPU optimizer assertions. Do not import or execute that native fixture
or wrapper on the Mac, including platform-skip paths.

If a test uses generated stand-ins, call it an integration-ordering fixture, not
the complete runtime executing WorkerRun. Independently reviewed full runtime,
dependency and source handoff plus integrated worker/supervisor admission remain
required before actual target-host binding, original S3 checkpoint restoration,
exact-data relocation, explicitly approved H100/CUDA validation and real SFT.
Later evaluation, rights/quality gates and deployment remain downstream.

No GPU/instance action, S3/SSH access, real model/data reads, inference, training,
promotion, dataset seal or registry mutation occurred. Mac work was small
source/lint/synthetic-test work only; existing native/CPU tests ran in GitHub CI.
No automation, background monitor, force push, cleanup of unrelated files or
deletion of previous failure evidence was performed.
